WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.053
A verified inventory needs ten capability entries. Each

00:00:04.139 --> 00:00:07.424
includes a supported verb, evidence, the check and

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.777
a limit. In this fictional example, the review

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.423
entry points to a draft containing an unsupported

00:00:12.551 --> 00:00:16.647
date and the corrected missing-information walkthrough. The improvement

00:00:16.689 --> 00:00:18.993
entry points to the specific correction and the

00:00:19.036 --> 00:00:22.593
revised result. They describe distinct actions, but each

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:26.262
must have support. An AI suggestion says the

00:00:26.305 --> 00:00:28.012
work saved ten hours and made the author

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:31.084
a certified consultant. Neither claim appears in the

00:00:31.127 --> 00:00:33.953
supplied evidence. Remove both. If one of your

00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:36.513
ten entries is missing its evidence, mark it

00:00:36.556 --> 00:00:39.713
pending and resolve it before final submission. Keep

00:00:39.798 --> 00:00:41.761
the same course work; do not fill a

00:00:41.803 --> 00:00:45.067
gap with an invented achievement. Practice explaining one

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:48.740
checked entry while showing the exact supporting artifact.
